  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fiber for the future, farming of abaca</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to transform the abaca (fiber) value chain in Mindanao (the Philippines) into a strong, efficient, resilient and future proof value chain that offers employment and a stable and diversified income to farmers and their communities.Abaca is grown and harvested for its fiber, which is primarily used in the paper industry, but also to make handicrafts.Abaca offers advantages like short gestation periods, multiple annual harvests, high demand and stable prices, while not requiring complex growing and post-harvest technologies.Abaca grows on higher elevations, allows for intercropping and benefits from shaded conditions under (existing upper) tree covers. As such, deforestation and warming trends can be countered.This will, among other things, result in:&#x2022;	5,000 smallholder abaca farmers with increased productivity and income; and&#x2022;	600 direct jobs supported.</narrative>
  </description>
